  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively point toward temperature-dependent mechanical and tribological testing of HEAs and toward dislocation, stacking-fault, HCP-fraction, and lattice-distortion changes as mediators. In particular, R1 and R13 show high-temperature dislocation reduction or annihilation and increased HCP fraction in a closely related FCC Cantor-type HEA, while R14 links elevated-temperature strength retention and eventual weakening to dislocation-based strengthening. R12 supplies the closest coating/wear context, and R18 supplies nanoindentation-based hardness and modulus measurement. However, no record combines a FeNiCrCoCu coating on Cu with temperature-controlled nanoindentation/friction simulation or predicts the specific threshold-like transition above about 900 K from stacking-fault deformation to lattice disorder with increasing friction. Constructing that combined intervention and mechanism would therefore require a substantial additional idea."
